<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH1e0877-en-633834e8" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Translation of 春秋公羊傳 into (English)</title><editor role="translator">Gentz</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="1">This work is in the public domain</availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Manuscript</title></bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH1e0877"><title xml:lang="och">春秋公羊傳</title></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#CH">Initially created: <date>2023-01-21T06:17:57.2+09:00</date> by CH</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH1e0877-start"><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:11.809+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:15.795+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:21.536+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:24.413+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:42.852+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:18:49.011+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:07.265+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:17.482+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:21.353+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:28.551+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:33.269+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:44.665+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:48.379+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-23a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:19:51.547+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:46:13.198+09:00">Ninth year, spring.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:46:34.879+09:00">Ji Jiang of Ji was sent to her marital home in the Royal Capital.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:14.227+09:00">If the wording “Queen” of the previous record “gives full realization” to the fact that for the King there is no Exterior,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:38.803+09:00">why does this record designate her as “Ji Jiang of Ji”?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:47:46.071+09:00">From our Lu perspective we speak in Ji’s voice.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:06.76+09:00">When Ji parents refer to their daughter,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:19.118+09:00">even though she has become Heaven’s Queen,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-29a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:48:36.557+09:00">they would still call her “our Ji Jiang.”</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:12.404+09:00">so the wording of the record gives full realization to this! </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:27.049+09:00">For the King there is no “Exterior”,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:41.361+09:00">In this case, why is she called “Queen”?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:49:57.007+09:00">When a bride is in her natal state she is called “daughter”.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:15.799+09:00">Therefore, if we approved of acting as a go between, then the great officer could, on the basis of our approval, use this approval to proceed on to Ji to meet the bride.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:06.321+09:00">The Son of Heaven directed us to act as a go between.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:33.466+09:00">In what way did the completion of his mission depend on us?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:51:49.439+09:00">The completion of his mission depended on us.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:04.833+09:00">In this case, why does the record say “subsequently”?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:19.143+09:00">A great officer must not initiate a subsequent undertaking.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:31.67+09:00">It indicates an ensuing undertaking.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:52:47.036+09:00">What does “subsequently” indicate?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-12T03:53:27.823+09:00"> In the ritual of marriage, the groom is not designated.  [the principal person is not mentioned (as the principal agent)]</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:01.06+09:00">Who is the Duke of Zhai?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:15.818+09:00">He was one of the Three Ministerial Dukes of the Son of Heaven.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:54:31.684+09:00">Why is he not designated as being dispatched?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T05:55:32.615+09:00"> The Duke of Zhai came.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-28a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-12T03:39:53.243+09:00">Subsequently, he went to receive the Queen in Ji. ["welcome" gets the meaning better than the cold "receive"]</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:15:56.202+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:01.158+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:04.368+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:08.243+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:19.669+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:27.76+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:33.476+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:37.607+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:41.516+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:46.631+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:51.107+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:16:54.733+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-11a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:17:03.1+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:06.151+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:10.65+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:14.522+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:18.109+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:22.181+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:28.877+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:33.43+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:36.37+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:41.258+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:46.026+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:07:55.969+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:00.518+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:03.379+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:06.857+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:13.185+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:18.086+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:24.717+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:08:55.282+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:03.555+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:08.189+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:11.575+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:29.959+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:34.842+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:45.512+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:49.208+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:09:59.473+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:02.982+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:07.036+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:14.527+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:19.315+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:23.284+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:29.329+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-8a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:10:35.134+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:01:01.635+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:01:07.443+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:01:12.416+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:03:36.377+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:03:43.981+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:03:50.481+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:03:55.222+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:03:59.95+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:04:04.601+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:04:10.157+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:04:15.655+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:04:20.392+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-2a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2026-04-24T05:04:33.503+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:02.929+09:00"> Someone from Jin seized the Marquis of Wei</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:27:57.413+09:00">What does “returned him to” indicate?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:08.773+09:00">and returned him to the Royal Capital.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:35.629+09:00">What does “he was returned to” indicate?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:28:46.745+09:00">“Returned him to” indicates guilt had already been determined;</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:08.048+09:00">“He was returned to” indicates guilt had not yet been determined.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:39.096+09:00">So why, in another record, where the guilt has not yet been determined, could the seizing qualify as an overlord’s punishment?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:29:52.39+09:00">“Returned him to” (in the present record) indicates</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:07.296+09:00">that a person was seized at the behest of the Son of Heaven,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:21.166+09:00">so whether or not he was determined to be guilty,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:34.971+09:00">can be deduced.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:30:51.994+09:00">“He was returned to” (in the other record)</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:12.063+09:00">indicates that a person was not seized at the behest of the Son of Heaven,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:21.889+09:00"> so whether or not he was determined to be guilty,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T06:31:39.662+09:00">cannot be deduced.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:03.933+09:00">What was the Marquis of Wei’s crime? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:11.04+09:00">He killed Shuwu.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:41.359+09:00">Why was this not recorded? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:32:51.722+09:00">To respectfully conceal the killing for the sake of Shuwu. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:01.826+09:00">The Chunqiu conceals for the sake of the worthy. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:09.643+09:00">What was worthy about Shuwu? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:21.385+09:00">He yielded the state. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:33:27.94+09:00">How is it that he yielded the state?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:04.062+09:00">Lord Wen of Jin expelled the Marquis of Wei and installed Shuwu. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:23.262+09:00">If Shuwu had declined to be installed and another had been established in his stead, </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:33.877+09:00">he feared that the Marquis of Wei would not be able to return. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:47.202+09:00">Consequently, Shuwu set himself up as lord</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:34:57.437+09:00"> and subsequently availed himself of the meeting at Jiantu to manage the return of the Marquis of Wei to his state. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:07.997+09:00">After the Marquis of Wei had been able to return,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:41.476+09:00">“Shuwu usurped my position.” </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:30.418+09:00">he declared,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:35:52.433+09:00">Yuan Xuan disputed this, saying, </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:04.207+09:00">“Shuwu is innocent!”</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:14.757+09:00">In the end, the Marquis of Wei killed Shuwu </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:29.605+09:00">and Yuan Xuan fled and left the state. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:36:58.277+09:00">This was Marquis of Jin, </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:08.714+09:00">why does it designate him as “someone”? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:16.808+09:00">To degrade him. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:25.329+09:00">Why degrade him? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:34.215+09:00">The disaster in Wei was Lord Wen’s creation. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:42.826+09:00">How did Lord Wen precipitate it? </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:37:52.331+09:00">When Lord Wen of Jin expelled the Marquis of Wei to install Shuwu, </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:02.891+09:00">he caused an elder and younger brother of another state to suspect one another, </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:11.84+09:00">effecting the murder of a maternal younger brother. </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_005-88a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T07:38:16.898+09:00">It was Lord Wen of Jin who did this!</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:11:50.95+09:00">The Zheng Heir Apparent Hu, resumed his position upon returning home to Zheng.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:13:12.952+09:00">Why do records sometimes say “assumed his position of rulership upon returning home” and sometimes say “resumed his position of rulership upon returning home”?  </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:12:34.466+09:00">Why is he designated “Heir Apparent”?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:12:40.606+09:00">It indicates the proper succession was restored.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:13:35.562+09:00">“Resumed his position of rulership upon returning home” indicates the departure was condemnable but the returning home was not condemnable.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:13:50.956+09:00">“Resumed his position of rulership upon invading” </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:14:10.208+09:00">indicates the departure was not condemnable but the entering was.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:14:19.518+09:00">“Assumed the position of rulership upon invading” </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:14:34.062+09:00">indicates the departure and the entering were condemnable.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-48a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:14:44.302+09:00">“Assumed the position of rulership upon returning home” </seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_002-49a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:14:50.854+09:00">indicates the departure and the entering were not condemnable.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-12T01:20:04.202+09:00">Summer, fourth month. 【: instead of . recommended everywhere, by the way]</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:48:54.054+09:00">Gongzi Bi of Chu assumed the position of rulership upon returning home from Jin to Chu</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:49:11.253+09:00">and assassinated his ruler Qian in Ganxi.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-12T01:13:17.442+09:00">This is a case of assassinating one’s ruler. [the reigning ruler]</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:50:16.283+09:00">Why does the record speak of “assuming the position of rulership upon returning home”? (see Huan 15.5)</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:50:32.018+09:00">Assuming the position of rulership upon returning home was not condemned in relation to the assassination of the established ruler.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-12T01:19:24.196+09:00">Why was assuming the position of rulership upon returning home not condemned in relation to the assassination of the established ruler?   [why is it that the returning to his rightful office was not disapproved of on account of the assassination and the establishing himself as a ruler?]</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:50:59.705+09:00">King Ling of Chu was a wayward ruler.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:51:11.376+09:00">When he built the Platform of Ganxi,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:51:22.118+09:00">three years passed and still he had yet to complete the project!</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:51:35.293+09:00">Consequently, Gongzi Qiji of Chu coerced Bi into being established as ruler.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:51:45.677+09:00">Whereupon he issued an order to the Ganxi laborers saying:</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:51:55.407+09:00">“Bi has been established as the ruler.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:52:11.382+09:00">Anyone who lingers, will not be allowed to return to their fields and hamlets.”</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T05:40:54.274+09:00">Subsequently, droves of laborers quit and left Ganxi. 【Leave out "subsequently"】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:52:50.084+09:00">King Ling then hung himself and died.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:53:06.883+09:00">Gongzi Qiji of Chu assassinated Gongzi Bi.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T06:13:41.348+09:00">Bi was already established as the ruler,  【Bi being already established as a ruler】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:53:48.252+09:00">so why is he designated as “Gongzi” (Lord’s Son)?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:53:59.31+09:00">He did not intend to usurp rulership.</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:54:35.15+09:00">If he did not intend to usurp rulership,</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-11T01:54:44.88+09:00">why is the assassination of the ruler ascribed to him?</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T06:19:45.5+09:00">It was Bi’s righteous obligation to consider it appropriate to commit himself to death rather than being established as the ruler. 【I think there is no such thing as a "righteous obligation" in English.】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T06:23:02.728+09:00">A great officer who kills another great officer is designated as “someone”.   【they are referred to as a person (without any indication of a title)】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T06:24:37.626+09:00">In this case, why is Qiji referred to by his personal and lineage name with regard to this assassination? 【in the context of】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_010-39a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2025-12-11T06:25:35.3+09:00">To imply that he planned to become the next ruler as a consequence of this assassination.  【this indicates that he was about to, from this point onward, to become the ruler】</seg><seg corresp="#CH1e0877_CHANT_001-9a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="20